<title>USA: Schering-Plough sees 1997 EPS in mid-teens.</title>
<headline>Schering-Plough sees 1997 EPS in mid-teens.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schering-Plough said Wednesday its increase in 1997 earnings per share should be in the &quot;mid-teens&quot;, which is a rise from its predictions early in the year of 1997 earnings per share in the &quot;low-to-mid teens.&quot;</p>
<p>The company also said its 1997 research and development spending will be about $810 million. Its 1996 research and development spending was $723 million.</p>
<p>Schering-Plough is a pharmaceutical company.</p>
</text>
